        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ನಾಗರಿಕ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾಗರಿಕ — nāgarika — \"a citizen\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಬ್ಬ ನಾಗರಿಕನೂ ತೆರಿಗೆ ಕಟ್ಟಬೇಕು. pratiyobba nāgarikanū terige kaṭṭabēku. Every citizen must pay taxes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ನಾಗರಿಕರು, nāgarikaru."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "As an adjective it means civil, civilised."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾಗರಿಕ (nāgarika) is borrowed from Sanskrit nāgarika, \"born or living in a town, civic\" (Monier-Williams), from nagara, \"a town\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
